      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#liebermann"/>Eallum Cristenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebyrað swiðe rihte, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hig haligdom<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ hadas ⁊ gehalgode Godes hus æfre swiþe georne griðian ⁊ friðian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.2"/>, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.3"/> hada gehwylcne weorðian be mæðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="284" ed="#liebermann"/>Eallum Cristenum mannum gebyrað swyðe rihte, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hig halido<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ⁊ hadas ⁊ gehalgode Godes hus æfre swyðe georne griðian ⁊ fryðian, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hy hada gehwylcne weorðian be mæðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="284" ed="#liebermann"/>Christianis omnibus sincere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.1-2"/> conuenit sanctuaria et ordines et Deo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.2-2"/> dicata loca summa discretione, tota deuotione pacificare, custodire, uenerari iuxta modum singulorum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="285" ed="#liebermann"/>Omnibus igitur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.1-4"/> Christianis iustissime decet (cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.2-3"/>) summa diligentia semper<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.3-2"/> uenerari<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.4"/> reliquias sanctorum, ordinatos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.5"/> et domos sanctificatas et unumquemque ordinem secundum mensuram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_4.lnote.oe.6"/> et uitam suam honorare.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="285" ed="#liebermann"/>Omnibus Christianis oportet rectissime, ut sacra et ordines et sanctificatas domos semper diligentissime pacificent et tutentur, ordinem unumquemque honorent secundum modum ipsius.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="158" ed="#robertson"/>Eallum Cristenum mannum gebyrað swiþe rihte, þæt hig haligdom ⁊ hadas ⁊ gehalgode Godes hus æfre swiþe georne griðian ⁊ friðian, ⁊ þæt hi hada gehwylcne weorðian be mæðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="236" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Eallum Cristenum mannum gebyrað swiðe rihte, þæt hig haligdom and hadas and gehalgode Godes hus æfre swiþe georne griðian and friðian, and þæt hi hada gehwylcne weorðian be mæðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_4.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="285" ed="#liebermann"/>Allen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_4.lnote.de.2"/> Christenmenschen geziemt sehr gehörig, dass sie Heiligthum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_4.lnote.de.3"/> und Geistliche und geweihte Gotteshäuser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_4.lnote.de.4"/> stets recht eifrig mit Sonderschutz befrieden, und dass sie jeden der [Klerus]stände nach dessen Range<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_4.lnote.de.5"/> ehren.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It very rightly befits all Christian people always to protect and keep the peace of relics and men in orders and consecrated houses of God most eagerly, and to honour each order according to its rank.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_4.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="159" ed="#robertson"/>It very justly befits all Christian men to maintain very zealously at all times the security and sanctity of holy things<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_4.robnote.n.2"/>, and of the members of the clergy, and of the consecrated houses of God, and to honour each member of the clergy according to his rank.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="237" ed="#rabin-doml"/>It very properly befits all Christians to always very zealously ensure the peace and sanctity of holy places, of those in orders, and of consecrated houses of God, and to respect all persons in orders according to their rank.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="285"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_18">VIII Atr 18</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VIII Atr. 18</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Had_1-1">Had 1.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:Had_1-3">Had 1.3</ref>; <ref target="clause:Grith_28">Grið 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Had_1-1">Had 1.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 4: Had. 1:1, 1:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Had_1-3">Had 1.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 4: Had. 1:1, 1:3</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 18.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 285, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">284</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">halid. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">halid. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">284</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fryþ. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fryþ. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">284</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">284</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. s. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. s. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">284</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dedicata <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> D. d. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dedicata instead of D. d. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">un̄ c̄q; <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">un̄ c̄q; Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ergo <hi rend="italic">Di;</hi> itaque <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ergo Di; itaque Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. sa., ordinatos et d. sa. se. uen. <hi rend="italic">H Di Lb Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. sa., ordinatos et d. sa. se. uen. H Di Lb Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ordinationes <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ordinationes Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">285</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">su. et ui. ferentis <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">su. et ui. ferentis Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Kapitel führt nur Atr homiletisch im einzelnen weiter aus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The chapter merely develops Atr further in homiletic detail</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt in Had 1. 1, 3. Grið 28</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used in Had 1. 1, 3. Grið 28</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘heilige Örter’ Q und ‘Reliquien’ Inst zu eng; besser ‘holy things’ Thorpe, Toller, was Cons meint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘holy places’ Q and ‘relics’ Inst are too narrow; better ‘holy things’ Thorpe, Toller, which is what Cons means</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 2. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. u</hi>. II 40</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 2. <hi rend="italic">Cf. below</hi> II 40</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_4.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Persönliche Reinheit bedingt Inst aus; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Geistliche 17b. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. u</hi>. 6, 2a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst makes personal purity a condition; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Geistliche 17b. <hi rend="italic">Cf. below</hi> 6, 2a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_4.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VIII Atr. 18; <hi rend="italic">Hadbot</hi>, 1; 1, 3; <hi rend="italic">Be Griðe</hi>, 28.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_4.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Translated <hi rend="italic">sanctuaria</hi>, Q; <hi rend="italic">reliquias sanctorum</hi>, Inst.; <hi rend="italic">sacra</hi>, Cons.</seg></note>
